{"title":"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Same_Approach_as_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Same Approach as Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> elements, and set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> elements.  What is the smallest possible number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e08507f538f3c1bff2373118be8e1faf0d3d627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cup B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc7899edb29e9b2df8b36bb1e78c0264f416c86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 20\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 35\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 300$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"388\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e08507f538f3c1bff2373118be8e1faf0d3d627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cup B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> will be smallest if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is completely contained in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, in which case all the elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> would be counted for in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. So the total would be the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a4993b7a8a0f30a1a7848f6df6be96ba608b9d9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{20 \\ \\mathbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume WLOG that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0e8d5948cda3abc9d795d6ade0a26903d264e08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A={1, 2, 3, 4, \\cdots , 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45f26f60c43e91ddffa3e833d1665a70c884bc27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B={6, 7, 8, 9, 10, \\cdots , 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" />. Then, all the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would be redundant in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e08507f538f3c1bff2373118be8e1faf0d3d627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cup B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175f4ef73080cfcde22c948e1f6019b0f3abf674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cup B = 1, 2, 3, 4, \\cdots, 20 \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"311\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Same_Approach_as_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Same_Approach_as_Solution_1)\">Solution 3 (Same Approach as Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Same Approach as Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea68bbbcea525fe1daaba819a4780e2ef99691b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\supset B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f5451590e41b731933710d9f34b93b6dd2994139.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\supset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> in this case is the superset), then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e08507f538f3c1bff2373118be8e1faf0d3d627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cup B$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> will contain 15 of the same elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bcb439aa9a66ade9e1b10d1dbad6827690bf7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B \\subset A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6ffbe0cb0b8d47bd10eec85fb336adf7694f896.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\subset$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> in this case is the subset). Therefore our new set must contain 15 elements already variant in both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> as well as 5 additional elements only the superset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> contains, and so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a1933ce34d9f521166bab6a2d0b13c4f3d4ac111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15+5= \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=biR0pgefTCs&amp;t=2s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=biR0pgefTCs&amp;t=2s</a>\n</p><p>~piHard\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A\">2011 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href